<title>GERMANY: Mercedes earns profits from buses, transporters.</title>
<headline>Mercedes earns profits from buses, transporters.</headline>
<dateline>HANOVER, Germany 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mercedes-Benz AG, a unit of Daimler-Benz AG, is earning a profit from its business in transporters and buses, chief executive Helmut Werner said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Speaking at a press conference at a truck exhibition, Werner said the company still has a fight on its hands in the market for trucks over six tonnes.</p>
<p>He declined to provide any figures about sales or profits in the two truck market sectors.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
